{"availability":"available","full":"BaryoDev/barakoCMS","name":"barakoCMS","description":"A headless CMS suite for .NET","category":"Other","language":"C#","stars":6,"forks":6,"created":"2025-12-27T14:37:53Z","updated":"2026-10-04T09:14:07Z","license":"MPL-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://barakocms.com/","topics":["aspnetcore","cms","content-management-system","csharp","dotnet","dotnet-core","event-sourcing","fastendpoints","headless-cms","marten","multi-tenant","nextjs","postgresql","rbac"],"demo":"https://playground.baryo.dev/barakocms-api%60","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:39.145Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:39.145Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:39.145Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:10.640Z","stars":6,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:39.145Z","stars":6,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Model it in barakoCMS. Edit it in barakoBrew. Render it with barakoPress. Deploy it anywhere.","BarakoCMS is a headless, API-first CMS built on FastEndpoints and Marten (event sourcing over PostgreSQL). The core stays small and generic; everything else, from accounting and analytics to email, file storage and auth providers, ships as opt-in modules you compose per project, and it's multi-tenant out of the box.","This repository is the API, and its own surface is Swagger (/swagger, on when Swagger:Enabled is true). The console that sits on top of it is barakoBrew, in its own repository at BaryoDev/barakoBrew, published from that repository as ghcr.io/baryodev/barako-brew. Before barakoBrew 1.2.0 the image was barako-admin, and that name is still pushed alongside it until barakoBrew 2.0.0. This repository has no front end."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"69d322a1bf5a6466b7765fb85d28cfffcdce8af6761f7a35ecb2890a58cb7116","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:10.747Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T05:51:40.499Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Model it in barakoCMS. Edit it in barakoBrew. Render it with barakoPress. Deploy it anywhere.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"analytics, Resend email, social sign-in, and the rest without touching the compose.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The console on top of it, at , is barakoBrew's playground; sign in as demoadmin / BarakoDemo2026!.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"JSONB with GIN indexing is what makes a runtime-defined content bag queryable at all, and PostgreSQL can be self-hosted on most platforms with no database licence fee, which matters for something people deploy themselves.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Two things run next to the app rather than inside it, so they do not appear in any manifest here: Umami is a separate self-hosted service that the Analytics.Umami module talks to over HTTP, and Caddy is the reverse proxy that terminates TLS in docker-compose.prod.yml.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"69d322a1bf5a6466b7765fb85d28cfffcdce8af6761f7a35ecb2890a58cb7116","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T05:51:40.500Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T09:14:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BaryoDev/barakoCMS/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T05:51:40.502Z","hash":"69d322a1bf5a6466b7765fb85d28cfffcdce8af6761f7a35ecb2890a58cb7116","originalBytes":32647,"storedBytes":32647,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","on